  <ChildComponent />
  <AnotherChildComponent />
</MyComponent>
```

In this example, `MyComponent` is using `React.cloneElement` to modify the existing child elements' props. This is useful when you want to manipulate the props of the child components without changing the original component.

In summary, use `React.cloneElement` when you need to modify the existing element's props or add new child elements to the existing component, and pass properties directly when you just want to pass props to a component.

